Expected elements: present

The presence check passes, including the two items that failed last round. The scrubber is present at 1440px — a 160px track at x672–832 with a filled head — and the position readout `128 / 1315` is a separate element beside it, both legible. Provenance is the `DATA` row of the Transaction pane, first labelled row, with a `Synthetic demo data` badge and the producer's sentences; there is no band above the identity bar. `CODE` with the current position on line 32, `CALL TRACE | EVENT LOG` with Call Trace open and seven frames, `VALUES` with eleven values, both stepping directions in the bar.

The monospace is doing its job: one code face, one tabular ACIR column, one tabular value column, line numbers right-aligned.

Four typographic problems. The provenance paragraph is set flush-right over eleven lines — the page's only body prose and its most important claim, given its least readable setting. FEE PAYER and TARGET wrap 66-character hashes into a 17-character right-aligned column, orphaning `32` and `4c` on third lines. The gutter's `⊘`/`⊙`/`·` triple encodes ran, did-not-run and unmarked in ~7px glyphs separated by an interior stroke. And the `+3`/`+2` overflow chips break the code listing's line rhythm at lines 26, 48 and 49.

Fixes: set the DATA paragraph flush-left; truncate the two addresses at a byte boundary rather than wrapping them.

Rating: 6/10

